Subject: [PATCH 11/11] chore: pre-commit hooks mirroring CI, Conventional
 Commits check, CONTRIBUTING.md
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

.pre-commit-config.yaml runs the same pinned tools CI runs — ruff check/
format, mypy against the baseline, vulture, eslint (errors), tsc, the
compiled-.js twin check — as local `system` hooks so there is one copy of
each version (requirements-dev.txt / package.json). The commit-msg hook is
scripts/check-commit-message.py: Conventional Commits with the project's
type list, <= 100-char subject, lowercase description, no trailing period,
blank line before the body; git's own Merge/Revert/fixup! subjects pass.
scripts/tests/test-commit-message.sh covers it and joins the scripts-tests
CI job automatically.

ruff.toml gains `force-exclude = true` so alembic/versions stays excluded
when pre-commit passes file names explicitly.

CONTRIBUTING.md: setup, branch and MR rules from the remediation plan,
every gate with the command and what to do when it fails, dependency
workflow (lock regeneration), where shared code lives.

